 program\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\nCongress\nHemaSphere\nAbout EHA\nSearch\nJoin EHA\nLogin\nExtending the reach of EHA Grants\nHome\nResearch & Innovation\nGrants\nEHA Research Grants\nExtending the reach of EHA Grants\nLeft Sidebar\n1 min read · May 6, 2025\nMay 6, 2025\nShare\nEHA Research Grants\nHow to apply for an EHA Research Grant\nEHA Research Grant review and selection process\nExtending the reach of EHA Grants\nWhat an EHA Research Grant covers\nTo ensure our whole community benefits from funding opportunities, we’ve created opportunities across diverse grants categories for researchers based in countries less-represented among EHA grantees.\nThe eligible countries are:\nAlbania\nArmenia\nAzerbaijan\nBosnia and Herzegovina\nBulgaria\nCroatia\nEstonia\nGeorgia\nHungary\nKosovo\nLatvia\nLithuania\nMoldova\nMontenegro\nNorth Macedonia\nPoland\nPortugal\nRomania\nSerbia\nSlovakia\nSlovenia\nTürkiye\nUkraine\nEHA Research Grants\nEHA Kick-off Grants\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grants\nShare\nEHA Research Grants\nHow to apply for an EHA Research Grant\nEHA Research Grant review and selection process\nExtending the reach of EHA Grants\nWhat an EHA Research Grant covers\nJoin EHA\nFull membership\nJunior membership\n60-day trial\nGet involved\nCareer development\nScientific meetings\nAbout us\nMission and vision\nJobs\nSponsor EHA\nContact us\nFollow us\nPrivacy statement\nTerms and conditions\nSubscribe\nCopyright © 2026\nBecome an EHA Mentor\nEHA Mentorship Program\nDiscover the rewards of mentoring\nApply by October 29\nApply today",
